## The 23.5 GB on the VRAM card — where it goes

Measured 2026-11-01 on the heretic boot. The card's **"Experts in VRAM 12.0 GB" is one line item, not the
model**: `nvidia-smi` reads 23,791 / 24,564 MiB, and the desktop's per-process table splits that as `strata`
**20.3 GiB** (Compute) + `strata-vision` **1.44 GiB** (its own context, carrying the 866 MB BF16 mmproj) +
the desktop **~0.8 GiB visible** (kwin 69 + lact 86 + brave 359 + plasma-shell 215 MiB… the list is longer).
Inside the `strata` process (GiB): expert cache **11.98** (`/metrics expert_cache_mib 12270` — 4,227 of
18,432 slots, so a hot 21% of the 57.30 GiB of routed experts, the rest over PCIe); resident non-expert
weights **5.07** (attn/GDN 2.23 + token emb/out 1.45 + norms, router, hyper-connections, indexer 1.39,
parsed from all 8 shards' tensor-info tables); MTP module **0.77**; resident KV **0.38** (32,768 positions ×
12 full-attention layers × 2 kv heads × (256+256) int8 — `full_attention_interval: 4` of 48 blocks); the
reserve **0.72** (`vram_free_mib 741`); and ≈ **1.4** of CUDA context, cuBLAS workspaces, prefill scratch
(`prefill_cap 19968`) and GDN states ×7 pool workers — **that last figure is a residual by subtraction, not
an engine itemization.** Two tables cost no VRAM at all: the 51,881 MB PLE/n-gram file (`--ple-io direct`)
and the 26.8 GiB `per_layer_token_embd.weight` (IQ4_NL, shape [160, 320,001,536]) ride the **71,150 MiB CPU
arena** (`/metrics arena_mib`) beside the experts — that is why this box wants 125 GB of RAM, and why PCIe
is on the monitor.

