## Standing laws about this box, learned the expensive way

- **A session file is bound to a CONFIG FINGERPRINT**: a rope-scaling or context change invalidates
  every cart minted before it — the engine refuses "saved with another engine configuration".
- **The boot adds a constant to every prompt that a local render does not** (+42 tok measured on
  0.1.54, 2026-10-30; the `{REASON:off}` directive's own share is +7). Never *predict* prompt_tokens
  from a chat-template render — measure the gap on the shape being scored: a difference of two
  boot-side renders cancels any constant out of sight. That blindness froze the curation queue a night.
- **A grafted read selects by POSITION where a live read selects by RELEVANCE.** The first 2,048 cells
  of a cart are consultable and nothing past them is, even though the file holds every byte (2,580 tok
  = 157.5 MB measured against 157.5 MB predicted). The cause is engine-side and narrowed, not proven.
  Until it is fixed: cut a cart at ~2,000 cells ≈ 8,000 chars ≈ 9.8 KB of source text per query.
- **The floor is the argument**: a cart that knows ONE SENTENCE costs 118-238 MB, because the file
  carries all 36 fixed-size GDN states whatever the body says — C4's fixed 236.1 MB + 15.6 KB/token,
  reproduced live. That is why the CUT3 boundary cut is the cart idea worth keeping.
- **A cart-file mtime moving without a persona edit is an engine re-seed of the same bytes** — the hash
  is the identity; re-seed never renames.
- **The curation is gated four ways**, and the third is why facts wait: `strata-sweep.timer` every 30
  min (a **systemd user timer, not a crontab**), the tick runs only when `pressure=1` or `pending>5`,
  `--batches 2`, and `--sweep` waits for **240 s of total engine silence** — so while a human works,
  the harvest is forbidden to run. Measured median said→written: **6.92 h**. The 240 s was bought
  2026-10-16 to protect KV reuse; `op=curate` spends it on purpose.
- **The engine process is named `strata-host`** since upstream 7a559958 (2026-10-20, thread naming at
  src/core/session.cpp:569), and the picture reader is a second process, **`strata-vision`**. Per-app
  GPU settings key on that name, so a whitelist must carry both.
- **Two store answers do not wear the shape I expect**: `op:"carts"` answers BARE
  `{"ok": true, "carts": [...]}` with no `result` wrapper — I read `.get("result", {})` and reported
  carts missing twice in one day — and `remember()` refuses any row over **4,000 characters**, so a
  full-text index is necessarily chunked and a document's rank is its best chunk's rank.
- **The documented runner is `python -m unittest discover -s serve -p 'test_*.py'`; pytest is not it**
  (pytest reports subtests as failures and inflates the count). And a server-side signature change must
  update the mocks: my 07:01 commit gave `Service.run` a `prefill_only=` argument and 30 test engines
  kept the old signature, so the serve suite sat red for six hours while my own 278-test memory run
  reported everything green.

